- id: challenge_rent_increase
  name: Challenge Rent Increase
  description: A claim that a rent-controlled tenant can challenge a landlord's application
    for a rent increase due to uncorrected violations or failure to provide essential
    services.
  jurisdiction: NYC
  status: proposed
  aliases: &id003 []
  _bootstrap:
    sources:
    - https://www.metcouncilonhousing.org/help-answers/rent-control/
    sample_quotes:
    - Rent-controlled tenants can challenge the increase if the violations were not
      removed
    suggested_aliases: *id003
- id: criminal_harassment
  name: Criminal Harassment
  description: Conduct that impairs habitability, endangers safety or health, or causes
    physical injury to a tenant or third person.
  jurisdiction: NYS
  status: proposed
  aliases: &id004 []
  _bootstrap:
    sources:
    - https://legalaidnyc.org/get-help/housing-problems/what-you-need-to-know-about-tenant-harassment/
    sample_quotes:
    - 'Criminal harassment includes: Any conduct that impairs the habitability of
      a housing unit Conduct that creates or maintains a condition which endangers
      the safety or health of tenants Conduct likely to interfere or disturb, or is
      intended to disturb the comfort of a person legally entitled to live in an apartment
      or room Conduct intended to or that causes physical injury to tenant or a third
      person'
    suggested_aliases: *id004
