- id: fair_market_rent_appeal
  name: Fair Market Rent Appeal
  description: A tenant's right to challenge the initial rent set at the start of
    rent stabilization, seeking a refund if the rent increased excessively.
  jurisdiction: NYS
  status: proposed
  aliases: &id019 []
  _bootstrap:
    sources:
    - https://hcr.ny.gov/rent-stabilization-and-emergency-tenant-protection-act
    sample_quotes:
    - The fair market rent guideline provided that a tenant has the right to file
      a fair market rent appeal with the Division of Housing and Community Renewal
      ('DHCR') to seek a refund if his or her rent increased by more than 16% between
      January 1, 2019 and July 30, 2022.
    suggested_aliases: *id019
- id: fraudulent_deregulation
  name: Fraudulent Deregulation
  description: A claim that a landlord improperly removed a unit from rent stabilization
    through fraud, such as false statements about vacancy or improvements.
  jurisdiction: NYS
  status: proposed
  aliases: &id020 []
  _bootstrap:
    sources:
    - https://www.courtlistener.com/opinion/9492811/gourin-v-72a-realty-assoc-lp/
    - https://www.courtlistener.com/opinion/10472015/matter-of-140-25-ash-assoc-llc-v-state-of-new-york-div-of-hous/
    - https://www.courtlistener.com/opinion/4632516/john-kuzmich-v-50-murray-street-acquisition-llc-william-t-west-v/
    - https://www.courtlistener.com/opinion/10131664/matter-of-aidekman-v-state-of-ny-div-of-hous-community-renewal/
    - https://www.courtlistener.com/opinion/4678184/matter-of-gray-v-new-york-state-div-of-hous-community-renewal/
    - https://www.courtlistener.com/opinion/4393779/trust-for-the-benefit-of-goldstein-v-lipetz/
    - https://www.courtlistener.com/opinion/4858343/united-states-v-skelos/
    - https://www.courtlistener.com/opinion/4865090/people-v-dr-226-holdings-llc/
    sample_quotes:
    - plaintiffs alleged that the rent was fraudulently deregulated
    - The scheme involved the use of bribery to secure rent-stabilized apartments
      and to facilitate the deregulation of units.
    - The issue in these appeals is whether the four-year lookback period for rent
      overcharge claims under the Rent Stabilization Law applies to claims of fraudulent
      deregulation.
    suggested_aliases: *id020
